    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38098" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-tĕro</span></b> , trīvi,
		3, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to rub off</i> or 
			<i>wear down in front</i> (ante-class. and in postAug.
			prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anum lima praeterunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Men. 1, 1, 9</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 11, 37,
			63</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To rub down beforehand</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oleum amygdali amari praetritum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
						Aur. Acut. 1, 17, 169</span></i>
			.</div>
